2026-11-06T03:09:01.7885586Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7894859Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7895906Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7896727Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7897216Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7897548Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7897967Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7898359Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7899415Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7899663Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7899868Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7900310Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7900529Z 
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7900825Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:09:01.7901598Z   $ sh ./install-nix
